  "Number": 13,
  "Question": "Which of the following is equal to\n\n\\[\\frac{9}{7 \\times 53}?\\]",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(\\dfrac{0.9}{0.7 \\times 53}\\)",
    "B": "\\(\\dfrac{0.9}{0.7 \\times 0.53}\\)",
    "C": "\\(\\dfrac{0.9}{0.7 \\times 5.3}\\)",
    "D": "\\(\\dfrac{0.9}{7 \\times 0.53}\\)",
    "E": "\\(\\dfrac{0.09}{0.07 \\times 0.53}\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "A",
  "Solution": "A quotient stays the same when its numerator and denominator are both divided by the same nonzero number. Divide both by \\(10\\). Since dividing the factor \\(7\\) by \\(10\\) divides the whole product \\(7\\times53\\) by \\(10\\), we obtain\n\\[\n\\frac{9}{7\\times53}\n=\\frac{9\\div10}{(7\\times53)\\div10}\n=\\frac{0.9}{0.7\\times53}.\n\\]\nThis is choice A.",
